## API Authorization

All protected endpoints require a valid JWT token from Keycloak. The JWT middleware validates:
1. Token signature (RS256)
2. Token expiration
3. Required role claim (from `roles` claim or `project_ids` claim)
4. Per-path role requirements defined in gateway config

## RBAC Flow

```
Client → Nginx → JWT Middleware (validate + extract roles)
                               ↓
                         Admin Gateway (check path + role)
                               ↓
                         Backend Service
```

## Keycloak → Gitea Mapping

| Keycloak Role       | Gitea Team       | Team Permission |
|--------------------|------------------|-----------------|
| platform-admin     | maintainers      | admin           |
| project-admin      | maintainers      | admin           |
| project-member     | developers       | write           |
| (no role)          | viewers          | read            |

## Notes

- Multi-tenant isolation enforced at API level via `project_ids` JWT claim
- Gitea organization permissions automatically synced via Ansible
- All admin access requires platform-admin role by default
- Project admins can be elevated via RBAC matrix update
